WEBVTT

02:29.903 --> 02:32.405
[Episode 4: Playing with Fire]

02:32.405 --> 02:33.934
[Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol & CTO James]
[A friendship beyond partnership]

02:33.934 --> 02:38.453
[Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol]
James is a groundbreaking innovator in AI.

02:38.453 --> 02:39.949
We pulled out all the stops to get him.

02:39.949 --> 02:40.975
["Three visits"]
[Haemu's future in tech innovation]

02:40.975 --> 02:44.384
First of all, thank you so much for having me.

02:46.518 --> 02:47.546
Thank you.

02:47.546 --> 02:51.540
You know, I truly feel like Mr. Jeon...

03:02.518 --> 03:05.615
She's probably at the office already, right?

03:05.615 --> 03:07.932
Let's stay out of her way today.

03:18.824 --> 03:20.829
Oh hey! Morning, Mr. Noh!

03:20.829 --> 03:22.595
Funny running into you right here!

03:22.595 --> 03:24.683
Small office, huh?

03:24.683 --> 03:25.917
Mr. Noh, it's your lucky day!

03:25.917 --> 03:27.127
Let me buy you a morning coffee.

03:27.127 --> 03:28.184
- No, I'm...
- What do you want?

03:28.184 --> 03:29.725
Americano? Latte?

03:29.725 --> 03:32.767
Are you an iced coffee die-hard?

03:32.767 --> 03:34.580
I'm the same way.

03:41.767 --> 03:44.615
How is she so unfazed right now?

03:44.615 --> 03:46.929
I know she saw me.

04:01.453 --> 04:02.755
All right,

04:02.755 --> 04:05.123
keep it together.

04:05.123 --> 04:07.947
Nice and easy.

04:07.947 --> 04:10.119
Same as always.

04:57.518 --> 04:59.168
Go!

05:00.720 --> 05:01.725
Go!

05:01.725 --> 05:03.392
That James guy...

05:03.392 --> 05:05.809
He's been all over the media.

05:05.809 --> 05:08.854
Sure, landing him was your crowning moment.

05:08.854 --> 05:11.430
Can we just shoot? No shop talk.

05:12.892 --> 05:14.670
Go!

05:16.027 --> 05:17.728
Go!

05:19.697 --> 05:21.060
So close!

05:21.060 --> 05:23.531
The last shot nearly hit the mark.

05:23.531 --> 05:27.101
I'm too rusty to even pull the trigger.

05:27.101 --> 05:28.873
The rifle is pretty heavy.

05:28.873 --> 05:30.035
Should we switch you to a pistol?

05:30.035 --> 05:31.835
Shooting at targets is no fun.

05:31.835 --> 05:34.892
Nothing worth hunting just sits there.

05:34.892 --> 05:38.591
Dad's literally a born sniper.

05:38.591 --> 05:41.261
The first time you took me hunting...

05:41.261 --> 05:43.305
I swore to myself right then.

05:43.305 --> 05:45.421
You're a terrifying man, so...

05:45.421 --> 05:47.643
I'd better keep my head down.

05:48.725 --> 05:50.928
Oh, come on.

05:51.553 --> 05:53.231
Why don't you guys go head to head?

05:53.231 --> 05:55.474
Show me what you've got for once.

06:21.718 --> 06:23.853
That must've been a total battlefield.

06:23.853 --> 06:26.903
People worried they'd turn on each other.

06:26.903 --> 06:30.683
So it's decision time for real.

06:30.683 --> 06:33.235
Who do we root for?

06:33.235 --> 06:35.892
But really it all comes down to who

06:35.892 --> 06:37.904
Ms. Joo decides to back, right?

06:37.904 --> 06:40.278
But she doesn't seem like she'd pick sides.

06:40.278 --> 06:42.614
She's way too principled for that.

06:42.614 --> 06:44.157
Mr. Ahn.

06:44.157 --> 06:46.942
On my way, ma'am!

06:56.122 --> 06:57.404
How am I supposed to act normal?

06:57.404 --> 06:59.288
Nothing about this feels normal.

07:00.506 --> 07:03.131
What kind of art class has no security?

07:03.131 --> 07:04.792
If they're running a class like that,

07:04.792 --> 07:08.130
they've got to lock the door.

07:10.224 --> 07:14.193
The Lim Ha Kyung case at the main R&D lab,

07:14.193 --> 07:17.497
they want to handle it internally?

07:17.497 --> 07:19.859
Yes, since it's straightforward,

07:19.859 --> 07:22.309
the lab's HR team runs the probe,

07:22.309 --> 07:25.606
and HQ only reviews the results.

07:26.738 --> 07:27.898
Let's handle this ourselves.

07:27.898 --> 07:29.517
- I'm coming along.
- Okay.

07:29.517 --> 07:30.850
Wait, what?

07:30.850 --> 07:33.164
You're going out there yourself?

07:33.164 --> 07:35.725
After James joined that R&D center,

07:35.725 --> 07:39.476
they glammed it up like Silicon Valley.

07:39.476 --> 07:41.798
I want to see it for myself.
And get some fresh air, you know?

07:41.798 --> 07:44.968
I've got meetings lined up today.

07:44.968 --> 07:47.214
Oh, is that so?

07:47.214 --> 07:50.932
Okay, in that case...

07:50.932 --> 07:54.551
Anyone want to tag along to the lab?

07:58.683 --> 08:01.892
Teams 1 and 2 are tied up with audits.

08:01.892 --> 08:03.778
We don't have anyone free.

08:03.778 --> 08:06.434
Oh, that makes sense.

08:06.434 --> 08:07.949
Okay,

08:07.949 --> 08:11.569
anyone on Team 3 not on an audit?

08:12.205 --> 08:13.767
Sorry, I've been having stomach issues

08:13.767 --> 08:16.476
from all the stress lately.

08:16.476 --> 08:18.909
Oh no, that's rough.

08:21.683 --> 08:24.498
Is there really no one?

08:40.106 --> 08:43.184
This is driving me crazy.

08:43.892 --> 08:45.529
Fine,

08:45.529 --> 08:48.564
I'll just face this head-on.

08:50.116 --> 08:54.162
- You know...
- The weather's so nice today, isn't it?

08:54.162 --> 08:55.698
Yeah, but ma'am...

08:55.698 --> 08:58.850
How about some udon at the rest stop?

08:58.850 --> 09:00.959
I remember a spot
with killer broth somewhere...

09:00.959 --> 09:04.392
It was near one of those bounce house spots.

09:04.392 --> 09:07.842
- Yesterday...
- Please don't make me talk.

09:07.842 --> 09:11.098
I really need to concentrate when I'm driving.

09:11.098 --> 09:13.683
I'm bad at multitasking. Talking throws me off.

09:13.683 --> 09:16.592
So let's keep it quiet, okay?

09:17.518 --> 09:19.866
- But still...
- I told you, no talking.

09:19.866 --> 09:22.848
Look! I nearly blew past the exit!

09:24.317 --> 09:27.237
You're the one doing all the talking...

09:36.207 --> 09:39.166
Company card violation, 57,250 won.

09:39.166 --> 09:41.325
Four attendance infractions.

09:45.812 --> 09:48.683
Go ahead and look it over once more.

09:48.683 --> 09:49.967
Got it.

09:49.967 --> 09:52.054
[Personal use of a corporate card]

09:52.054 --> 09:54.421
Who did you get on the bad side of?

09:56.683 --> 10:00.472
- Sorry?
- Anyone can see this is a targeted audit.

10:00.472 --> 10:02.481
The stuff about misusing a company card,

10:02.481 --> 10:04.440
that's all too dated to explain away now.

10:04.440 --> 10:05.817
Five or ten minutes of tardiness?

10:05.817 --> 10:07.819
A quick trip to the bank,

10:07.819 --> 10:10.771
that doesn't get flagged to HQ for attendance.

10:12.407 --> 10:16.613
What on earth did you do
to rub someone the wrong way

10:16.613 --> 10:20.468
that a fourth-year senior researcher
ended up a target?

10:23.334 --> 10:25.169
Audit is an independent department.

10:25.169 --> 10:27.547
No need to walk on eggshells. Talk to me.

10:27.547 --> 10:30.082
Confidentiality is guaranteed, obviously.

10:39.559 --> 10:42.302
Actually, I...

10:43.184 --> 10:46.142
Hey, what's going on here?

10:46.142 --> 10:48.434
Everybody, nice to meet you all. I'm James.

10:48.434 --> 10:49.683
- Hi, James. Nice to meet you.
- Hey.

10:49.683 --> 10:51.070
Nice to meet you.

10:51.070 --> 10:53.198
You know, I've actually heard a lot about you.

10:53.198 --> 10:56.236
I've been wanting to see you,
Head of Audit Joo.

10:56.236 --> 10:59.809
Apologies, James,
but we're in the middle of the meeting.

10:59.809 --> 11:00.809
I see that.

11:00.809 --> 11:03.166
Oh my gosh, what did you do?

11:03.166 --> 11:06.142
Ms. Joo. Ha Kyung is such a nice girl.

11:06.142 --> 11:08.226
Take it easy on her, okay?

11:08.226 --> 11:09.255
Alright, so...

11:09.255 --> 11:10.351
Hurry up, let's wrap it up!

11:10.351 --> 11:13.767
What about some coffee in my office?

11:13.767 --> 11:14.802
Sounds good?

11:14.802 --> 11:15.642
- Okay, sure.
- Yeah.

11:15.642 --> 11:17.351
Alright. I'll see you there.

11:17.351 --> 11:19.840
- Perfect. Let's go guys.
- Bye.

11:27.649 --> 11:29.516
Go ahead and sit down.

11:35.309 --> 11:37.850
That thing you wanted to tell us before,

11:37.850 --> 11:39.818
do you want to keep going?

11:44.749 --> 11:47.392
I've got nothing to say.

11:47.392 --> 11:51.163
I'll admit to everything.

12:02.184 --> 12:04.351
Coffee's here.

12:04.351 --> 12:05.395
Oh, thank you.

12:05.395 --> 12:07.512
- A hot Americano, right?
- Thank you.

12:07.512 --> 12:09.373
- Go on, have some.
- Thank you.

12:09.373 --> 12:11.721
I'll have...

12:11.721 --> 12:12.735
This is really good.

12:12.735 --> 12:14.445
- So this is that famous...
- Mr. Hong?

12:14.445 --> 12:16.364
- Yes, it's really good.
- When are you submitting

12:16.364 --> 12:17.353
Team 1's quarterly expense report?

12:17.353 --> 12:18.934
Hae Young.

12:18.934 --> 12:20.624
Let it go today. It's Children's Day.

12:20.624 --> 12:21.633
It's Children's Day?

12:21.633 --> 12:24.100
It means the Head of Audit is out today.

12:24.100 --> 12:29.618
- When the boss is gone, we run the show.
- We run the show.

12:30.434 --> 12:33.358
She's away, so I'm planning
to take a half-day this afternoon.

12:34.048 --> 12:35.883
Are you out of your mind?

12:35.883 --> 12:37.300
Look at Assistant Manager Yoon.

12:37.300 --> 12:38.860
She already dropped
her half-day plan for today.

12:38.860 --> 12:41.922
Using PTO on a day like this is just a waste.

12:43.057 --> 12:44.226
Right.

12:44.226 --> 12:46.820
I've still got so much to learn.

12:46.820 --> 12:48.680
- When do I need to...
- Hello.

12:48.680 --> 12:51.100
Excuse me.

12:51.100 --> 12:53.899
To what do we owe the honor of your visit?

12:53.899 --> 12:55.689
Yeah, well...

12:55.689 --> 12:57.990
I had to come say hello to our Audit folks.

12:57.990 --> 13:00.184
You guys hold all the power around here.

13:00.184 --> 13:03.070
Where's our Haemu celebrity, Head of Audit Joo?

13:03.070 --> 13:04.890
She's out on a field visit right now,

13:04.890 --> 13:06.163
but it shouldn't take long,

13:06.163 --> 13:09.600
- so she should be back before the evening.
- Oh, really?

13:09.600 --> 13:12.795
When she's back,
how about a surprise group dinner?

13:12.795 --> 13:15.548
They say gizzard shad is in season.
How about some with soju?

13:15.548 --> 13:17.634
It's on me!

13:22.514 --> 13:24.891
Alright, find a place and send me a message.

13:24.891 --> 13:28.677
- Will do. Thank you.
- Thank you.

13:32.434 --> 13:34.442
I should have taken that half day.

13:34.442 --> 13:37.929
This would be his first dinner
since he returned to HQ, right?

13:37.929 --> 13:40.336
Man, our boss doesn't even need to network.

13:40.336 --> 13:41.863
The connections come to her.

13:41.863 --> 13:45.027
- Impressive.
- Oh shoot, I need to update her.

13:53.081 --> 13:54.870
Excuse me.

13:59.642 --> 14:03.526
I don't think you got to finish
what you wanted to say.

14:03.526 --> 14:05.855
If it feels awkward talking inside the company,

14:05.855 --> 14:08.342
how about we chat somewhere outside?

14:11.767 --> 14:14.095
We have a phrase in the Audit Office.

14:14.095 --> 14:17.260
We call it
"Investigate, examine, decide, defend."

14:17.260 --> 14:18.861
We investigate like cops,

14:18.861 --> 14:20.154
examine like prosecutors,

14:20.154 --> 14:22.324
judge like a court would,

14:22.324 --> 14:25.048
and protect tipsters like defense attorneys.

14:25.702 --> 14:28.843
If you have something
you'd like to come forward with,

14:28.843 --> 14:30.600
from that moment,

14:30.600 --> 14:33.335
we become your defense team.

14:33.335 --> 14:35.202
So,

14:36.059 --> 14:38.121
it's okay to put your faith in us.

14:39.007 --> 14:41.582
You still work for the company, though.

14:41.582 --> 14:43.053
It was the same thing back then.

14:43.053 --> 14:45.805
"Trust us and lay it all out," they said.

14:45.805 --> 14:47.506
I'm sorry?

14:54.843 --> 14:56.598
Wait!

14:59.151 --> 15:00.164
It's me.

15:00.164 --> 15:02.263
Mr. Noh, you with Ms. Joo?

15:02.263 --> 15:03.822
She's not answering her phone.

15:03.822 --> 15:06.283
She's not with me right now.

15:06.283 --> 15:08.411
I'll get back to you.

15:08.411 --> 15:10.163
Alright.

15:10.163 --> 15:12.039
Mr. Noh.

15:12.039 --> 15:16.128
Come quick! There's a ton of cool stuff here!

15:23.926 --> 15:25.136
James!

15:25.136 --> 15:26.472
There you go!

15:26.472 --> 15:28.759
How did you even make something like this?

15:28.759 --> 15:31.809
James, are you an alien?

15:31.809 --> 15:33.351
Secret.

15:33.351 --> 15:35.220
We're seriously questioning it too.

15:35.220 --> 15:37.360
The way he thinks is just next level.

15:37.360 --> 15:39.859
Exactly. He learned Korean in no time.

15:39.859 --> 15:41.979
He's literally a genius.

15:41.979 --> 15:44.625
Oh come on, you're laying it on thick.

15:44.625 --> 15:47.450
- James, your Korean is great!
- I know.

15:47.450 --> 15:48.786
Oh, In Ah.

15:48.786 --> 15:50.525
Do you play golf?

15:50.525 --> 15:51.683
Of course.

15:51.683 --> 15:52.955
Okay, because...

15:52.955 --> 15:54.750
Last-minute dinner
with the Managing Director Jeon.

15:54.750 --> 15:56.083
Notify Ms. Joo.

15:56.083 --> 15:58.711
- How about a 100,000 won bet?
- Excuse me.

15:58.711 --> 16:00.017
James, don't forget.

16:00.017 --> 16:03.226
I'm from the audit department.

16:03.226 --> 16:05.400
No money. But...

16:05.400 --> 16:08.909
how about the loser gets a forehead flick?

16:08.909 --> 16:09.966
I know that.

16:09.966 --> 16:12.382
- Okay, deal.
- Deal.

16:15.094 --> 16:16.142
President Lee Seung Hyun

16:16.142 --> 16:19.158
is in New York preparing
for the second-half launch event.

16:19.158 --> 16:20.941
Managing Director Cheon of Group PR

16:20.941 --> 16:22.860
is working to control media coverage
on the leadership issue.

16:22.860 --> 16:25.113
He's been cozying up to journalists.

16:25.113 --> 16:26.697
Vice President Choi Woo Tae
from Chemical Division

16:26.697 --> 16:28.510
has reportedly received
a recruitment offer from a foreign firm.

16:28.510 --> 16:30.532
We're keeping an eye on it.

16:30.532 --> 16:32.393
How are things between Director Ma
and Director Han?

16:32.393 --> 16:34.580
They were in a power struggle
over choosing an accounting firm.

16:34.580 --> 16:36.666
Seems they came to an understanding.

16:36.666 --> 16:40.131
Word is they'll file it
through the Planning Office shortly.

16:40.131 --> 16:44.206
It seems Managing Director Jeon Seong Yeol
stepped in to mediate.

16:44.966 --> 16:46.760
Seong Yeol?

16:46.760 --> 16:47.885
Yes.

16:47.885 --> 16:49.875
Managing Director Jeon has been meeting
with key board members

16:49.875 --> 16:52.422
one by one lately.

16:53.474 --> 16:55.247
He's putting in the work.

16:55.247 --> 16:59.522
Tonight, he'll be at the Audit dinner.

16:59.522 --> 17:01.167
The Audit Office?

17:01.167 --> 17:02.483
Oh, this is killing me.

17:02.483 --> 17:05.277
Oh, Secretary Park,
what brings you to our humble corner...

17:05.277 --> 17:06.924
Hello.

17:06.924 --> 17:08.656
For the Audit dinner tonight,

17:08.656 --> 17:11.084
the Vice Chairman will be joining as well.

17:11.084 --> 17:12.975
Since the Vice Chairman doesn't do raw food,

17:12.975 --> 17:15.121
I'd recommend going with a meat restaurant.

17:15.121 --> 17:18.208
Also,
find somewhere with a solid wine selection.

17:18.208 --> 17:20.690
Email me the location once it's booked.

17:20.690 --> 17:22.444
I'll be off then.

17:22.444 --> 17:24.214
- Okay.
- Got it.

17:24.214 --> 17:26.164
Take care.

17:27.883 --> 17:29.593
Why are we suddenly

17:29.593 --> 17:31.564
the department everyone's interested in?

17:31.564 --> 17:33.100
Wait, MD Jeon...

17:33.100 --> 17:35.182
Oh, right!

17:35.182 --> 17:37.456
We booked a sashimi restaurant.

17:37.456 --> 17:39.318
MD Jeon wanted gizzard shad, so that's why.

17:39.318 --> 17:41.272
This is a total disaster.

17:41.272 --> 17:43.151
Oh, but wait...

17:43.151 --> 17:45.693
Setting up dinners is Team 3's job.

17:45.693 --> 17:48.280
Team 3 can figure it out then.

17:54.142 --> 17:55.871
Hey, guys.

17:55.871 --> 17:58.914
Are we seriously overthinking this?

17:58.914 --> 18:01.472
The MD said he wanted gizzard shad,

18:01.472 --> 18:03.878
and the Vice Chairman can't do raw food.

18:03.878 --> 18:06.422
Of course, a dietary limit beats a preference.

18:06.422 --> 18:07.716
Makes sense, right?

18:07.716 --> 18:10.141
So I'll just book a meat place.

18:13.518 --> 18:14.805
Sorry.

18:14.805 --> 18:16.725
This isn't as straightforward as you think.

18:16.725 --> 18:17.975
Hae Young,

18:17.975 --> 18:20.436
can you not see how critical this is?

18:20.436 --> 18:23.392
Our whole Audit Office's future
hangs on this menu choice.

18:23.392 --> 18:26.017
Don't rush into a decision.

18:26.017 --> 18:30.263
Since the MD asked first,
should we go with gizzard shad?

18:30.263 --> 18:33.398
The first invite does give us a good reason.

18:34.033 --> 18:36.495
Still, the Vice Chairman is the higher-up,

18:36.495 --> 18:39.446
isn't that a bit rude?

18:41.290 --> 18:43.825
This is my biggest work crisis ever.

18:48.974 --> 18:50.736
Nice.

18:52.309 --> 18:54.184
Bravo!

18:54.184 --> 18:56.338
Bravo!

18:59.809 --> 19:02.229
What are you doing right now?

19:02.229 --> 19:05.336
I'm telling you, there's more to this case.

19:05.336 --> 19:08.275
You suspected it was a targeted audit too!

19:08.275 --> 19:09.892
We have to dig into this the right way.

19:09.892 --> 19:11.184
Now is not the time for games.

19:11.184 --> 19:12.896
Here we go.

19:14.267 --> 19:16.616
Oh, nice shot!

19:19.161 --> 19:22.476
Can you not see
I'm working super hard right now?

19:22.476 --> 19:24.675
Nice, James.

19:25.975 --> 19:28.995
Right. Nice, James.

19:31.131 --> 19:32.559
- Are you next?
- Yes.

19:32.559 --> 19:35.210
Good luck. Let's go, In Ah.

19:37.975 --> 19:39.598
- Yeah.
- Mr. Noh.

19:39.598 --> 19:40.875
You didn't check your messages?

19:40.875 --> 19:42.434
Are we doing meat or gizzard shad?

19:42.434 --> 19:44.187
I just need one answer.

19:44.187 --> 19:46.805
What's keeping Ms. Joo so tied up?

19:47.774 --> 19:50.318
Right now she's...

19:50.318 --> 19:52.477
in a global-level competition.

19:53.362 --> 19:55.293
She's doing a global what?

19:55.293 --> 19:56.365
Well...

19:56.365 --> 19:58.184
Fine, got it.

19:59.326 --> 20:01.434
Still no answer again?

20:01.434 --> 20:03.947
We seriously need to book a place now.

20:04.832 --> 20:07.895
The stress is through the roof.

20:09.659 --> 20:12.006
Look. My hair is falling out from the stress.

20:12.006 --> 20:14.975
What am I going to do?

20:14.975 --> 20:16.600
Just...

20:16.600 --> 20:17.991
let's have both.

20:17.991 --> 20:19.410
The meat and the gizzard shad.

20:19.410 --> 20:20.870
What, like a buffet?

20:20.870 --> 20:22.184
I looked it up,

20:22.184 --> 20:25.187
and there's no place nearby that does both.

20:25.187 --> 20:26.883
No.

20:26.883 --> 20:29.699
The barbecue spot
from last year's year-end party,

20:29.699 --> 20:32.609
it's a BBQ joint, but the owner's mother-in-law
ships it from the coast,

20:32.609 --> 20:34.359
they also serve gizzard shad.

20:34.359 --> 20:36.488
Seasonal special menu.

20:36.488 --> 20:38.642
- Wait, really?
- Let me take a look.

20:38.642 --> 20:40.000
Found it!

20:40.000 --> 20:41.870
Let me take a look.

20:41.870 --> 20:43.715
Look at this.

20:45.289 --> 20:46.920
Da Ye, why are you bringing this up now?

20:46.920 --> 20:49.701
You should've told me before I lost my hair.

20:52.589 --> 20:55.591
Hey, it was a great time.
I actually had a lot of fun today.

20:55.591 --> 20:58.224
It was so much fun for me too.

20:58.224 --> 20:59.878
Also...

21:01.142 --> 21:03.182
I must say

21:03.182 --> 21:05.309
I'm rather impressed today.

21:05.309 --> 21:06.850
I really think you're a great leader.

21:06.850 --> 21:09.688
That's actually very flattering to hear.
Thank you.

21:09.688 --> 21:13.100
You have nearly 10,000 employees.

21:13.100 --> 21:14.309
And yet,

21:14.309 --> 21:16.904
you personally know
how to care for junior staff

21:16.904 --> 21:19.272
like Lim Ha Kyung.

21:20.574 --> 21:22.023
Yeah, I mean...

21:22.023 --> 21:23.620
What can I say...

21:23.620 --> 21:26.248
It's because I love my people.

21:26.248 --> 21:27.970
Give me a second.

21:34.004 --> 21:36.100
Ma'am. Our designated driver

21:36.100 --> 21:37.424
will take you back to Seoul.

21:37.424 --> 21:38.926
- Okay.
- Yeah.

21:38.926 --> 21:40.892
- Shall we go?
- In Ah, come visit me.

21:40.892 --> 21:43.309
Come here. I'm going to miss you.

21:43.309 --> 21:45.682
Of course, James.

21:45.682 --> 21:46.809
Take care, okay?

21:46.809 --> 21:48.336
See you soon.

21:48.336 --> 21:49.353
I'll see you.

21:49.353 --> 21:50.407
Alright.

21:50.407 --> 21:53.473
- Bye.
- Goodbye, James.

22:01.323 --> 22:03.892
Get in. Hurry!

22:03.892 --> 22:06.411
Please follow that car up ahead.

22:06.411 --> 22:07.975
- I'll pay double the fare to Seoul.
- Sure.

22:07.975 --> 22:09.656
Buckle up.

22:23.345 --> 22:25.272
I knew it.

22:26.600 --> 22:28.478
You're following James, right?

22:28.478 --> 22:29.600
Come on, fill me in already.

22:29.600 --> 22:31.351
What was today all about?

22:31.351 --> 22:34.733
That wasn't about bonding with James, was it?

22:34.733 --> 22:36.942
Back at the lab,

22:36.942 --> 22:41.196
I took a look at James's card usage history.

22:41.196 --> 22:44.366
[James's Personnel File]
The company set him up at Baron Hotel,

22:44.366 --> 22:47.725
but charges at Rosa Hotel kept popping up.

22:47.725 --> 22:50.831
Is that why you're suspicious of James?

22:50.831 --> 22:53.100
It was strange from the beginning.

22:53.100 --> 22:55.335
A young researcher like Ms. Lim
getting flagged for a targeted audit.

22:55.335 --> 23:00.184
But James, I mean, you know how it is.
Even if James is actually tied to this,

23:00.184 --> 23:02.600
the higher-ups will try to bury it.

23:02.600 --> 23:06.085
If this goes south,
there's no telling what they'll do to you.

23:06.085 --> 23:07.797
Exactly.

23:09.141 --> 23:11.259
I need to make sure I don't mess it up.

23:35.502 --> 23:37.186
Here.

23:40.184 --> 23:42.582
- Your check-in is complete.
- Thank you.

23:43.476 --> 23:45.251
Thank you.

23:47.597 --> 23:49.392
Mr. Noh.

23:49.392 --> 23:50.683
Run.

23:50.683 --> 23:52.767
What?

23:52.767 --> 23:54.600
We need to find out his room number.

23:54.600 --> 23:56.304
Hurry.

24:48.160 --> 24:50.076
He got on the elevator.

24:50.076 --> 24:51.943
Where are you?

24:53.120 --> 24:54.915
I'm on the fifth floor.

24:54.915 --> 24:56.354
Still?

24:56.354 --> 24:57.874
Run faster!

24:57.874 --> 24:59.575
What?

25:01.559 --> 25:04.122
Oh, come on.

25:14.059 --> 25:16.301
Ninth floor, tenth floor...

25:19.521 --> 25:20.971
Thirteenth floor.

25:20.971 --> 25:23.308
He got off on the thirteenth floor.

25:46.800 --> 25:50.090
Got it. Room 1307.

25:51.219 --> 25:54.014
Honey!

25:54.014 --> 25:55.057
Hurry up.

25:55.057 --> 25:57.008
Get in here, hurry!

25:58.018 --> 25:59.646
Get over here.

26:02.190 --> 26:04.997
Oh my, look at you all sweaty!

26:04.997 --> 26:08.102
Did you run here because you missed me so much?

26:11.267 --> 26:14.286
Yeah, honey.

26:14.286 --> 26:16.656
It's so hot.

26:17.267 --> 26:20.767
You two look so lovely together.

26:20.767 --> 26:22.387
How would you like your room?

26:22.387 --> 26:25.921
We have city view and park view.

26:25.921 --> 26:27.756
Room 1306, please.

26:27.756 --> 26:28.784
Pardon?

26:28.784 --> 26:31.553
Oh, actually...

26:31.553 --> 26:34.179
Today is our anniversary.

26:34.179 --> 26:38.351
Celebrating a special memory
we made in room 1306.

26:40.268 --> 26:42.309
One moment, please.

26:42.309 --> 26:44.180
- Sure.
- How lovely.

26:46.627 --> 26:47.734
This is awkward.

26:47.734 --> 26:51.696
Room 1306 is already booked,

26:51.696 --> 26:54.142
and the room next to it, 1307,

26:54.142 --> 26:57.411
was just reserved a moment ago...

26:57.411 --> 26:59.694
How about 1308?

27:00.622 --> 27:02.791
That one is available, but...

27:02.791 --> 27:05.210
Or since it's your anniversary today,

27:05.210 --> 27:07.476
we could upgrade your room

27:07.476 --> 27:09.840
to our hotel's signature suite...

27:09.840 --> 27:13.136
No, thank you, room 1308 please.

27:13.136 --> 27:17.208
That suite has an amazing view, though.

27:17.208 --> 27:19.701
I just want to stay...

27:21.269 --> 27:24.679
as close to that special room as possible.

27:31.683 --> 27:33.240
Please make it happen.

27:33.240 --> 27:36.649
That room means more to us than any suite.

27:37.786 --> 27:40.351
The memories are just too precious.

27:40.351 --> 27:42.934
Of course.

27:42.934 --> 27:46.701
Let me get you checked in right away.

27:48.421 --> 27:50.109
Right this way.

28:05.934 --> 28:07.642
Your acting was flawless up until now,

28:07.642 --> 28:09.932
so what's with the cold feet all of a sudden?

28:11.111 --> 28:13.188
You already saw everything anyway.

28:16.642 --> 28:18.983
Seriously.

28:45.185 --> 28:47.367
[Seasonal Gizzard Shad]

28:50.482 --> 28:53.653
How about seating the Vice Chairman
across from the MD?

28:53.653 --> 28:56.325
That makes the head seat thing awkward.
That won't work.

28:56.325 --> 28:57.584
What if we try this?

28:57.584 --> 28:59.032
Split the tables apart,

28:59.032 --> 29:01.434
shad section here, meat section there.

29:01.434 --> 29:03.625
Doesn't that stick out like a sore thumb?
Separating the two of them?

29:03.625 --> 29:05.622
- Right?
- Yeah.

29:05.622 --> 29:07.865
We're in trouble.

29:08.543 --> 29:10.523
Is everybody here already?

29:10.523 --> 29:13.267
You made it, Sir!

29:15.327 --> 29:18.635
How do we do the seating?

29:18.635 --> 29:21.348
Anywhere you're comfortable, sir.

29:26.019 --> 29:28.847
She's just being a typical Gen Zer.

29:35.809 --> 29:38.237
Alright, I'll take this spot.

29:38.237 --> 29:39.781
Actually, how about the center seat...

29:39.781 --> 29:42.492
No, I like it here. I can see all your faces.

29:42.492 --> 29:43.931
Let's shuffle seats as the night goes on.

29:43.931 --> 29:45.510
Oh, sure thing.

29:45.510 --> 29:46.811
The Vice Chairman just arrived.

29:46.811 --> 29:47.791
- Good evening, sir.
- Welcome, sir.

29:47.791 --> 29:49.510
- Good evening, sir.
- Good evening, sir.

29:49.510 --> 29:51.351
Seriously, you should be faster.

29:51.351 --> 29:53.661
We're practically dying of hunger.

29:58.787 --> 29:59.801
Have a seat, everyone.

29:59.801 --> 30:01.011
Sure.

30:01.011 --> 30:02.920
Sit down, everyone.

30:06.600 --> 30:07.642
Did you wait long?

30:07.642 --> 30:08.748
Not at all.

30:08.748 --> 30:11.559
We already ordered the food, so it's coming.

30:11.559 --> 30:12.600
Here's the wine list.

30:12.600 --> 30:14.628
See if anything catches your eye, sir.

30:14.628 --> 30:15.971
Are you kidding?

30:15.971 --> 30:17.568
Wine at a team dinner?

30:17.568 --> 30:20.031
We need soju for a work dinner, right?

30:20.031 --> 30:22.735
Yes, soju sounds great.

30:25.120 --> 30:26.934
Let everyone drink what they want.

30:26.934 --> 30:28.738
Sounds good.

30:30.457 --> 30:32.208
Where is In Ah? I don't see her.

30:32.208 --> 30:34.419
Yeah, I guess she's still downstairs.

30:34.419 --> 30:36.212
I'll call her right now to check.

30:36.212 --> 30:38.415
- Call Mr. Noh instead.
- Got it.

30:38.415 --> 30:40.258
Mr. Noh from our team is with her.

30:40.258 --> 30:43.669
Both of them are away on business.

30:47.434 --> 30:49.425
I'm burning up right now.

30:52.559 --> 30:55.523
Hey, what's with the striptease?

30:55.523 --> 30:58.109
Because you made me run up the stairs.

30:58.109 --> 31:00.238
So I'm sweating like crazy.

31:00.238 --> 31:02.016
This heat is killing me.

31:18.880 --> 31:19.932
It's me.

31:19.932 --> 31:20.998
Oh, hello.

31:20.998 --> 31:23.376
Are you with Ms. Joo?

31:25.138 --> 31:27.106
Yeah, hold on a second.

31:28.598 --> 31:30.758
Hyun Gyu wants to talk to you.

31:31.868 --> 31:32.884
What's up?

31:32.884 --> 31:34.184
Yeah, it's me.

31:34.184 --> 31:35.904
Where are you guys right now?

31:35.904 --> 31:38.196
I'm currently in a hotel room.

31:39.067 --> 31:41.600
Both the Vice Chairman and MD
are at the dinner.

31:41.600 --> 31:43.604
When do you think you can make it?

31:43.604 --> 31:45.907
I'm sleeping here.

31:45.907 --> 31:46.960
Sorry?

31:46.960 --> 31:48.904
Mr. Noh and I will miss the dinner.

31:48.904 --> 31:50.204
Send my regards to the executives.

31:50.204 --> 31:51.934
But, wait a minute...

31:51.934 --> 31:53.392
But...

31:53.392 --> 31:55.882
What did she say?

31:55.882 --> 31:57.252
Well, the thing is...

31:57.252 --> 32:02.382
She's in a hotel room with Mr. Noh.

32:02.382 --> 32:05.501
They plan on spending the night there.

32:06.136 --> 32:07.889
Both of them are sleeping there?

32:07.889 --> 32:09.755
Yes.

32:11.351 --> 32:13.004
Why would you word it like that?

32:13.004 --> 32:15.412
People are definitely going to misunderstand.

32:16.242 --> 32:18.984
We cannot tell them about investigating James.

32:18.984 --> 32:21.042
I only stated exactly what we're doing.

32:21.042 --> 32:23.947
I guess so, but...

32:23.947 --> 32:25.980
I hear something.

32:27.576 --> 32:29.268
What is it?

32:34.226 --> 32:36.504
He's taking a shower.

32:36.504 --> 32:37.767
What?

32:37.767 --> 32:39.824
Great, these walls are super thin.

32:39.824 --> 32:41.642
Take a seat over by me.

32:41.642 --> 32:43.330
Alright.

33:05.989 --> 33:08.147
Hold on, move over for a second.

33:09.991 --> 33:12.412
You just plop down anywhere, huh?

33:12.412 --> 33:14.127
Alright, right here.

33:31.059 --> 33:33.506
Man, I'm so thirsty.

33:50.727 --> 33:52.728
Oh, this looks pretty good.

33:52.728 --> 33:55.247
I'll open this instead of taking overtime pay.

33:55.247 --> 33:58.787
Are you seriously drinking in a hotel room now?

33:58.787 --> 33:59.791
Absolutely.

33:59.791 --> 34:02.409
Someone made me run, so I'm parched.

34:03.086 --> 34:04.227
What's the problem?

34:04.227 --> 34:06.664
You said we have no secrets left.

34:20.809 --> 34:24.148
That was a great meal. I'm stuffed.

34:24.148 --> 34:25.670
Thanks for the food.

34:25.670 --> 34:28.111
- It was delicious.
- Thank you for treating us.

34:28.111 --> 34:29.771
- Hey, Min Soo.
- Yes, sir?

34:29.771 --> 34:31.451
Let's play pool together sometime.

34:31.451 --> 34:33.491
I won't go easy on you.

34:33.491 --> 34:36.244
You have to follow me back on Instagram, sir.

34:36.244 --> 34:38.248
Sure, we might as well do it right now.

34:38.248 --> 34:39.831
For real? That's awesome.

34:39.831 --> 34:41.476
Please follow me, too.

34:41.476 --> 34:43.410
Hold on a second, guys.

34:43.410 --> 34:45.767
I absolutely love

34:45.767 --> 34:48.122
doing stuff like this.

34:48.767 --> 34:50.093
Love the sense of humor.

34:50.093 --> 34:52.267
Just hit follow for both of you.

34:52.267 --> 34:54.345
Actually, we should snap a quick picture.

34:54.345 --> 34:55.476
Sounds good.

34:55.476 --> 34:56.993
- Get in the frame.
- Hurry.

34:56.993 --> 35:00.467
- Say cheese. One, two, three.
- Get in here!

35:08.484 --> 35:10.086
- Mr. Choi.
- Yes.

35:10.086 --> 35:12.586
Please stop by a pharmacy for some aspirin.

35:12.586 --> 35:14.565
Understood.

35:23.118 --> 35:25.326
I'll go get it now.

35:33.518 --> 35:35.794
Tonight was just so childish.

35:46.892 --> 35:49.484
Is it uncomfortable for you

35:49.484 --> 35:52.144
that I have feelings for you?

35:57.160 --> 35:59.559
Look, right here.

35:59.559 --> 36:01.957
[Promissory Note]
Park Ah Jeong.

36:01.957 --> 36:04.535
[Park Ah Jeong]
You signed right there as the loan guarantor.

36:04.535 --> 36:06.042
And your personal seal is
stamped right here too.

36:06.042 --> 36:08.670
I don't know anything about that.

36:08.670 --> 36:10.142
This is a crime, what you're doing!

36:10.142 --> 36:12.090
It was your brother who committed the fraud.

36:12.090 --> 36:13.392
Even with the deposit,

36:13.392 --> 36:16.115
it doesn't cover half
of what that guy skimmed off.

36:16.115 --> 36:19.138
We gave him a good deal
since you work at a big company.

36:19.138 --> 36:21.715
How about you think about switching jobs
while you're at it?

36:21.715 --> 36:25.469
Someone like you could pay it all off
in just a month.

36:43.850 --> 36:45.781
Vice Chairman.

36:46.683 --> 36:48.145
Hello.

36:48.145 --> 36:49.518
I'm Park Ah Jeong,

36:49.518 --> 36:52.579
I was just assigned
to the secretariat last week.

36:54.934 --> 36:57.176
I had no idea you'd be here this late...

36:57.176 --> 37:00.571
I haven't actually gone home yet, to be honest.

37:00.571 --> 37:03.132
What brings you in this early, Ms. Park?

37:14.642 --> 37:18.647
This is my little escape
when I need some space for myself.

37:19.362 --> 37:20.825
I barely get to use it these days.

37:20.825 --> 37:22.693
Time just doesn't allow it.

37:24.831 --> 37:27.531
You're welcome to stay.

37:33.095 --> 37:35.831
It's pretty well stocked...

37:37.683 --> 37:39.070
But, there's nothing to eat.

37:39.070 --> 37:40.878
Not even water.

37:46.767 --> 37:48.677
Care for a drink?

38:07.723 --> 38:09.406
Have a seat.

38:14.559 --> 38:17.017
Let's just skip all the small talk

38:17.017 --> 38:18.883
and get right to it.

38:18.883 --> 38:21.383
Would you like to shower first?

38:21.383 --> 38:23.587
Should I go first?

38:24.934 --> 38:26.715
What's wrong?

38:27.663 --> 38:30.344
I guess you have different preferences.

38:52.593 --> 38:54.952
You can just take a kind gesture

38:58.059 --> 39:00.749
for what it is.

39:06.440 --> 39:09.207
If it really makes you uncomfortable,

39:09.207 --> 39:11.844
just think of it as an employee perk.

39:26.100 --> 39:29.620
The innovation in your product is impressive.

39:29.620 --> 39:32.518
But the mid-to-long-term roadmap

39:32.518 --> 39:35.409
feels a bit unclear to me.

39:36.388 --> 39:38.638
For Haemu's portfolio,

39:38.638 --> 39:40.631
great ideas matter

39:40.631 --> 39:43.667
but you'll need a solid execution plan too.

39:44.554 --> 39:46.295
Yeah.

39:46.888 --> 39:51.058
I'll check the Vice Chairman's schedule
and get back to you.

39:51.058 --> 39:52.759
Sure.

40:24.761 --> 40:26.747
I'm a little drunk.

40:27.683 --> 40:30.214
If you don't mind me asking,

40:32.975 --> 40:35.228
what's eating you up

40:35.228 --> 40:37.226
so much?

40:37.226 --> 40:39.600
Every day it's booze instead of food,

40:39.600 --> 40:42.193
no sleep, and all work.

40:42.193 --> 40:44.811
If I had that kind of money,

40:45.518 --> 40:48.607
I'd be eating well and living it up.

41:08.017 --> 41:09.827
That's a mistake.

41:09.827 --> 41:11.838
It's late. Go home.

41:13.059 --> 41:15.300
It's not a mistake.

41:17.434 --> 41:19.638
I have feelings...

41:20.559 --> 41:22.647
for you.

41:22.647 --> 41:24.727
This isn't the booze talking.

41:24.727 --> 41:27.088
And it's not about your money or status either.

41:27.088 --> 41:29.451
I don't want anything from you.

41:29.451 --> 41:31.809
I know your situation,

41:31.809 --> 41:34.027
and I know where I stand.

41:35.081 --> 41:37.011
I just

41:38.600 --> 41:41.070
wanted you to know

41:41.070 --> 41:42.786
how I feel.

41:44.518 --> 41:46.790
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

42:26.633 --> 42:28.653
I'm even more embarrassed

42:29.747 --> 42:31.668
about the art class thing.

42:33.346 --> 42:36.474
I went back and forth a million times,

42:36.474 --> 42:39.327
crawl in a hole and die

42:39.327 --> 42:41.678
or kill you.

42:42.850 --> 42:44.609
So you were just faking

42:44.609 --> 42:46.368
being cool about it.

42:59.654 --> 43:02.160
Sorry about that, though.

43:02.160 --> 43:04.654
I figured you'd feel
like your privacy got invaded.

43:04.654 --> 43:06.953
I crossed a line back there.

43:07.974 --> 43:10.774
You didn't even know it was my thing, so.

43:10.774 --> 43:12.459
Excuse me?

43:14.074 --> 43:16.475
Right, the art hobby.

43:16.475 --> 43:19.424
I mean, what are the odds
of running into each other like that...

43:23.270 --> 43:26.100
Just so you don't get the wrong idea
about a side job,

43:26.100 --> 43:27.455
I'm not getting paid for it.

43:27.455 --> 43:29.999
It's more of a personal outlet, really.

43:29.999 --> 43:31.948
Sure.

43:31.948 --> 43:34.743
A side job didn't even cross my mind.

43:34.743 --> 43:37.025
I was in no position to think that far...

43:46.683 --> 43:48.537
Still...

43:49.725 --> 43:51.748
Can I ask you something?

43:54.434 --> 43:56.795
Why you do it. The hobby.

44:01.094 --> 44:03.677
It's the only way I feel like I can breathe.

44:06.434 --> 44:09.628
Everyone in this field has something like that.

44:09.628 --> 44:11.988
You need at least one escape.

44:11.988 --> 44:14.190
So, yeah.

44:54.060 --> 44:57.218
How are your feet that tiny, though?

44:58.115 --> 44:59.608
My feet?

45:01.121 --> 45:03.424
Or are yours just weirdly big?

45:04.455 --> 45:06.698
I don't think so.

45:31.761 --> 45:33.361
Would you stop staring at me like that?

45:33.361 --> 45:34.601
What?

45:35.319 --> 45:38.184
I wasn't staring...

45:38.184 --> 45:39.975
Same here, honestly.

45:39.975 --> 45:43.077
It hit me pretty hard, mentally speaking.

45:43.077 --> 45:44.829
So my body shocked you?

45:44.829 --> 45:46.821
Yeah, it definitely did.

45:48.335 --> 45:50.017
No, what I mean is,

45:50.017 --> 45:52.336
it's not that it was bad or anything like that,

45:52.336 --> 45:54.257
what I'm trying to say is...

45:54.257 --> 45:57.634
- Like, in a good way...
- So you liked it?

45:57.634 --> 45:59.306
No, no, that's not it either,

45:59.306 --> 46:02.100
saying "liked it" could
come across the wrong way,

46:02.100 --> 46:04.181
what I'm actually trying to get at is...

46:04.181 --> 46:06.800
what I mean by that is...

46:10.725 --> 46:12.109
So what's your point?

46:12.109 --> 46:13.944
What do you want me to do with that?

46:13.944 --> 46:16.365
Should I just strip down right now?
To make it fair?

46:16.365 --> 46:18.417
- That actually sounds fine by me.
- Sorry?

46:18.417 --> 46:20.522
How could...

46:21.683 --> 46:24.025
Seriously...

46:25.122 --> 46:26.889
Watch it...

47:28.226 --> 47:29.786
Ha Kyung.

47:29.786 --> 47:31.509
Come on in.

47:36.630 --> 47:38.564
Have a seat.

47:42.267 --> 47:44.559
Come on.

47:44.559 --> 47:46.441
Sit down.

47:55.476 --> 47:57.809
The audit team's here from HQ.

47:57.809 --> 47:59.591
Because of you.

47:59.591 --> 48:02.415
Why make this harder than it has to be?

48:08.059 --> 48:10.642
What did you talk to those people about?

48:11.975 --> 48:14.678
You didn't dare mention my name, right?

48:16.309 --> 48:18.850
Okay, good. That's my girl.

48:18.850 --> 48:21.238
Okay, good.

48:21.238 --> 48:24.979
Hey, Ha Kyung, don't cry.

48:27.309 --> 48:30.562
It hurts me to see this, okay?

48:30.562 --> 48:32.600
Let's keep this smooth.

48:32.600 --> 48:34.540
No need to make it ugly.

48:34.540 --> 48:37.367
You little piece of...

48:39.518 --> 48:40.809
We're not done.

48:40.809 --> 48:43.373
You stay here. Don't say a word. Okay?

48:44.559 --> 48:46.418
Who is it?

48:48.309 --> 48:50.725
- In Ah.
- Hi, James.

48:50.725 --> 48:52.590
What are you guys doing here?

48:57.019 --> 48:59.142
Are you out of your mind?

48:59.142 --> 49:03.600
- What the...
- I won the flick bet, fair and square.

49:03.600 --> 49:06.896
That wasn't a flick, though.
That was a full-on punch.

49:22.683 --> 49:25.206
He said he wanted to meet about work.

49:25.888 --> 49:28.918
Something about questions on the research data.

49:29.723 --> 49:32.848
The hotel location did bother me a little,

49:32.848 --> 49:35.270
but James was staying at a hotel,

49:35.270 --> 49:39.598
and I'd heard he held
a lot of meetings there...

49:41.148 --> 49:42.717
I made a bad call.

49:42.717 --> 49:45.238
You didn't do anything wrong.

49:45.238 --> 49:47.270
Don't be so hard on yourself.

49:49.281 --> 49:51.286
[Haemu Electronics CTO James]
What do you think you're doing?

49:51.286 --> 49:52.993
We were following orders. That's all.

49:52.993 --> 49:54.518
This is so unfair.

49:54.518 --> 49:56.437
It's James, ma'am.

49:56.437 --> 49:58.156
James...

50:08.809 --> 50:09.968
Thank you.

50:09.968 --> 50:11.220
Don't thank me.

50:11.220 --> 50:13.796
The audit team did its job. That's it.

50:43.503 --> 50:45.829
No wonder you're wiped out.

51:15.683 --> 51:17.725
There's something I've been wondering about.

51:17.725 --> 51:20.017
Back when the affair
involving Deputy Manager Son came out,

51:20.017 --> 51:22.374
both Son and Jung were equally at fault,

51:22.374 --> 51:25.464
but you only kept Son at HQ.

51:25.464 --> 51:28.212
You said he was more valuable to the company.

51:28.212 --> 51:29.683
That corporate ethics work differently,

51:29.683 --> 51:33.525
and that all that matters is
what you gain or lose.

51:33.525 --> 51:35.345
James is on a completely
different level from Son,

51:35.345 --> 51:37.222
and he's critical to this company,

51:37.222 --> 51:39.924
so why go this far?

51:41.351 --> 51:43.332
How is that even a question?

51:43.332 --> 51:45.263
It's a crime.

51:50.781 --> 51:52.942
He's waiting for you.

51:54.659 --> 51:56.042
Mr. Noh, wait here.

51:56.042 --> 51:57.927
I'll handle the briefing.

52:10.850 --> 52:14.843
You really warmed up to each other.

52:14.843 --> 52:16.017
I mean,

52:16.017 --> 52:19.059
you're standing here like a guard dog
watching over his owner.

52:19.059 --> 52:20.974
And this is after all that trash-talking.

52:20.974 --> 52:22.967
Why are you picking a fight?

52:24.106 --> 52:26.008
It's bugging me.

52:26.008 --> 52:28.598
You stayed out all night without a single text.

52:29.733 --> 52:30.904
It wasn't "staying out."

52:30.904 --> 52:32.852
That's my place.

53:50.184 --> 53:51.606
You're home late.

53:51.606 --> 53:53.474
Want a drink?

53:59.683 --> 54:02.436
Hey, what's your Vice Chairman's deal?

54:02.436 --> 54:05.203
He seemed so put-together.

54:05.203 --> 54:09.142
Honestly, I'd never seen
that side of him either,

54:09.142 --> 54:10.376
but it's James, so.

54:10.376 --> 54:11.955
Still, come on.

54:11.955 --> 54:13.670
He sexually assaulted someone under him,

54:13.670 --> 54:16.173
and when she reported it, he turned around
and targeted her with an audit.

54:16.173 --> 54:19.217
James or Zeus, doesn't matter.
He deserves to be out.

54:19.217 --> 54:21.197
Why are you getting so fired up about this?

54:21.197 --> 54:24.518
Since when were you so big on justice?

54:24.518 --> 54:26.476
This isn't about justice.

54:26.476 --> 54:29.095
I'm talking about basic common sense.

54:29.797 --> 54:32.930
Speaking of common sense, though,

54:34.027 --> 54:36.796
last night in that hotel room,

54:36.796 --> 54:42.337
what exactly were you and In Ah
doing all night?

54:42.337 --> 54:43.678
What's wrong?

54:43.678 --> 54:45.327
Think about it. Realistically,

54:45.327 --> 54:49.110
a man and a woman
spending the night at a hotel together,

54:49.110 --> 54:50.990
doesn't that seem off?

54:57.047 --> 54:59.251
We worked. That's what we did.
Can't you tell from what came out of it?

54:59.251 --> 55:00.631
We caught something huge.

55:00.631 --> 55:02.222
Sure, you worked.

55:02.222 --> 55:06.089
But was that seriously all that happened?

55:07.208 --> 55:09.827
Nothing else at all?

55:14.159 --> 55:15.150
Something happened, didn't it?

55:15.150 --> 55:17.115
Nothing happened.

55:17.115 --> 55:18.767
You're saying something so out of nowhere

55:18.767 --> 55:21.270
that my brain just stalled for a second.

55:23.725 --> 55:25.983
What's your deal?

55:26.642 --> 55:28.595
Go shower and get to bed.

55:52.105 --> 55:55.054
Here's the final report on the James case.

56:12.834 --> 56:15.285
This is a little...

56:15.285 --> 56:18.345
Okay,
if you look at the audit scope right here...

56:18.345 --> 56:20.037
Sure.

56:21.548 --> 56:23.512
Right here...

56:33.768 --> 56:35.941
It really does look good on you.

56:38.434 --> 56:40.516
It meant a lot.

57:22.112 --> 57:24.655
[You've got mail]
[Subject: "Reporting Head of Audit Joo In Ah"]

57:31.826 --> 57:32.869
[Joo In Ah's carrying
on an inappropriate relationship at work]

57:32.869 --> 57:33.889
[Attached is the proof]

57:36.706 --> 57:37.999
[Joo In Ah's carrying
on an inappropriate relationship at work]

57:37.999 --> 57:39.024
[Attached is the proof]

58:16.184 --> 58:17.947
Mr. Noh.

58:19.767 --> 58:21.522
You're skipping the club today?

58:21.522 --> 58:24.078
It's not even a sketching session today.

58:25.505 --> 58:29.217
And I don't think I made this clear before,

58:29.217 --> 58:31.722
you showing up is fine by me.

58:31.722 --> 58:33.513
The sketching thing only happens
every once in a while,

58:33.513 --> 58:36.850
and I just don't have to model if you're there.

58:36.850 --> 58:38.643
I'm fine.

58:38.643 --> 58:39.733
That's what I'm saying.

58:39.733 --> 58:42.138
So just come without overthinking it.

58:49.100 --> 58:50.867
It's not that simple for me.

58:50.867 --> 58:53.024
And there's no reason for me to be there.

59:07.392 --> 59:08.934
Hey.

59:08.934 --> 59:10.925
You can't drink here.

59:10.925 --> 59:13.094
You're being that guy right now.

59:13.094 --> 59:15.463
It's non-alcoholic, okay?

59:16.089 --> 59:19.383
So what are you even doing here?

59:23.850 --> 59:25.559
I don't know.

59:25.559 --> 59:27.025
There's nobody to talk to.

59:27.025 --> 59:29.239
You seriously have no friends?

59:29.239 --> 59:31.149
That's kind of sad.

59:32.184 --> 59:34.642
You want to grab a drink with me?

59:34.642 --> 59:35.784
Yeah, not happening.

59:35.784 --> 59:38.449
You can't just trust every guy you meet

59:38.449 --> 59:39.996
and drink with them like it's nothing.

59:39.996 --> 59:41.164
You need to have some boundaries.

59:41.164 --> 59:42.729
Being this fearless
in a foreign country, honestly.

59:42.729 --> 59:44.329
- Why are you taking it out on me?
- Excuse me?

59:44.329 --> 59:45.828
Things not going your way?

59:45.828 --> 59:47.257
What's going on?

59:47.257 --> 59:51.248
Still haven't figured out
who that pretty woman likes?

59:52.648 --> 59:55.169
I haven't figured out who exactly,

59:56.096 --> 59:57.477
but something's moving forward.

59:57.477 --> 59:58.765
No way.

59:58.765 --> 01:00:00.449
That's great, seriously.

01:00:00.449 --> 01:00:02.268
You said you need to find out who it is

01:00:02.268 --> 01:00:04.226
to keep your job in one piece.

01:00:04.226 --> 01:00:06.097
So, this is a good thing, right?

01:00:07.226 --> 01:00:09.016
Yeah.

01:00:09.642 --> 01:00:10.693
It's a good thing.

01:00:10.693 --> 01:00:12.451
Then how come you seem so annoyed?

01:00:12.451 --> 01:00:14.397
This is good news.

01:00:16.559 --> 01:00:18.021
I know.

01:00:20.314 --> 01:00:23.030
I can't even figure out why I'm irritated.
It's irritating.

01:00:41.725 --> 01:00:43.759
It meant a lot.

01:04:40.842 --> 01:04:43.374
Have I always looked like this?

01:04:44.682 --> 01:04:46.417
Apparently.

01:05:03.683 --> 01:05:05.562
You really are.

01:07:02.725 --> 01:07:04.824
A kiss means you're together.
That's just how it works.

01:07:04.824 --> 01:07:05.664
I owe you an apology.

01:07:05.664 --> 01:07:07.975
What I did crossed a line
no supervisor should ever cross.

01:07:07.975 --> 01:07:08.984
Like something just came over me.

01:07:08.984 --> 01:07:10.244
So that kiss was one-sided?

01:07:10.244 --> 01:07:11.584
How does that make any sense?

01:07:11.584 --> 01:07:12.949
Even after we kissed,

01:07:12.949 --> 01:07:16.059
I thought a sorry would
just wipe the slate clean.

01:07:16.059 --> 01:07:17.912
I want to know
if there's actually something between us.

01:07:17.912 --> 01:07:20.063
That's what I'm trying to figure out.

01:07:20.063 --> 01:07:21.559
Sleep with me and see?

01:07:21.559 --> 01:07:23.850
You up for that?

01:07:23.850 --> 01:07:25.461
Can it really happen just like that?

01:07:25.461 --> 01:07:27.518
You know, suddenly catching feelings

01:07:27.518 --> 01:07:30.123
for someone you've known before.
